# GREP_SUMMARY: platform-agent-watchdog systemd timer 30s poll interval oneshot unit activation
# STRUCTURE: ▶ OnBootSec(60s) → ▶ OnUnitActiveSec(30s) → ▶ activate platform-agent-watchdog.service → ⎋ repeat
#
# region MODULE_CONTRACT [DOMAIN(DevOps): Watchdog scheduling; CONCEPT(Timer): periodic polling; TECH(Systemd): timer unit]
## @purpose  Systemd timer that activates platform-agent-watchdog.service every 30 seconds for continuous self-update monitoring.
## @scope    Phase 04: ensures watchdog runs at regular intervals to catch agent self-update events.
## @invariants
##   - OnBootSec: 60s — delay after boot before first activation (allows Docker + agent to start)
##   - OnUnitActiveSec: 30s — re-activate 30 seconds after the service unit last became active
##   - Unit: platform-agent-watchdog.service — the oneshot unit to trigger
##   - WantedBy: timers.target — starts with all other systemd timers
##   - Timer is external to agent — survives agent crash (07 §6)
## @rationale
##   Q: Why 30s interval?
##   A: Balances responsiveness (detect self-update within ~30s) with system load. WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT=90s means
##      3 polling cycles fit within the timeout window — watchdog detects failure promptly.
##   Q: Why OnBootSec=60s?
##   A: Ensures Docker daemon and agent container have time to start before first watchdog check.
## @links_to_spec  plans/BRIEF/05-service-update.md §5
# endregion MODULE_CONTRACT

[Unit]
Description=Platform Agent Watchdog Timer — poll every 30s

[Timer]
OnBootSec=60s
OnUnitActiveSec=30s
Unit=platform-agent-watchdog.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
